                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_96">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Convent of Austin friars</orgName><p>Copied by Adam de
                        Stockton, lector in the Austin convent at Cambridge c. 1375: 'scriptus a
                        fratre Adam de Stocton lectore in conuentu Cantebrigie a.d. mccc
                        septuagesimo septimus' (p. 361), and in other places in the MS in other
                        years (BRUC 557).</p><p>'Liber iste pertinet fratri Roberto Mendham anno
                        domini MoCCCC nonagesimo vijo' (at end). [i.e. Robert Mendham OESA,
                        Cambridge convent in 1470--71; in 1508; BRUC 401--2.]</p><p>'Liber iste
                        pertinet fratri Thome Swyllyngton anno domini moccccco vo ita est per me
                        prescript'' (at end). [i.e. Thomas Swillington OP, Cambridge convent in
                        1408; BRUC 571.]</p><p>Also 'conuentus . . . . brigie', erased.</p><p> </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">John Dee (1527--1609), mathematician,
                     astrologer, and antiquary: 'Ioannes Dee 1561 Bostoniae' (fol. 5r). Dee's cat.
                     C, no. 7.</provenance>
